.SH NAME
anpu-serve - Browse scan history in a local read-only dashboard


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu serve [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
serve exposes the SQLite scan history as a read-only local web
dashboard: scan list, per-scan findings with evidence, and scan diffs.

.PP
Localhost-only by design: --addr must resolve to loopback (127.0.0.0/8,
::1, or localhost); anything else is refused. Only GET routes exist —
the dashboard can never modify history. For remote access, use an SSH
tunnel instead of exposing the port.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--addr\fP="127.0.0.1:8080"
	listen address, loopback only (host:port)

.PP
\fB--db\fP=""
	history database path (default ~/.anpu/anpu.db)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for serve

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	max scans on the index page


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


